# Repository line-ending policy (issue #2044).
#
# `text=auto` normalises every text file to LF in the index, and `eol=lf` writes
# LF into the working tree on every platform regardless of a contributor's
# core.autocrlf. That makes a checkout byte-identical on the Linux and Windows
# runners: a script that parses a text file by pattern (for example
# scripts/check-manifest-versions.mjs reading src-tauri/Cargo.lock) sees the same
# bytes everywhere instead of depending on the runner it happens to run on.
#
# `auto` rather than `text` so the `binary` rule below, and any binary a future
# change adds, keep their exact bytes.
#
# The two properties this buys are checked, not assumed: `npm run check:eol`
# fails when a tracked text file is stored mixed or CRLF in the index, and the
# rules below pin the files that must deviate.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows command interpreters need CRLF in the working tree, not in the index:
# `eol=crlf` keeps the stored form LF (so the index stays uniform and the gate
# above passes) while checkin/checkout gives cmd.exe and PowerShell the endings
# they need. Last match wins, so these follow the `*` rule.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Generated ts-rs bindings are written with LF (issue #359). Pin them to LF so
# the CI drift gate (`git diff --exit-code src/types/generated`) never trips on
# a CRLF/LF mismatch on Windows runners where core.autocrlf may be enabled.
# The harness catalog JSON snapshot (ADR-0037) is emitted by the same cargo
# test pass and must stay LF for the same reason.
# ts-rs also leaves a trailing space after a field that is followed by a doc
# comment. Regenerated output must not be hand-edited, so `git diff --check`
# (the harness whitespace gate) skips trailing-space errors for these files.
src/types/generated/*.ts text eol=lf whitespace=-trailing-space
src/types/generated/*.json text eol=lf
# Fuzz corpus seeds are exact byte streams: CRLF line endings, NUL bytes,
# invalid UTF-8, and at least one header value whose trailing space is the
# thing under test. `binary` is `-diff -merge -text`: it keeps any checkout
# from rewriting line endings (the pinned outcomes would then fail for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the reader) and stops `git diff --check`
# from reading that space as whitespace damage.
src-tauri/fuzz/corpus/** binary
